 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "The $\\ell$-adic Tate module is free of rank $2g$",
 "statement": "Let $A$ be an abelian variety ([def-sc-abelian-variety]) of dimension $g$ over an algebraically\nclosed field $k$ and let $\\ell\\ne\\operatorname{char}k$. Then\n\n$$\nT_\\ell A\\cong\\Z_\\ell^{2g},\\qquad V_\\ell A\\cong\\Q_\\ell^{2g}.\n$$",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-abelian-varieties/sk-prop-av-tate-rank/prop-av-tate-rank.md",
  "place": "node prop-av-tate-rank, order 591"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-sc-abelian-variety"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "By [lem-sc-ntorsion-etale] each level is\n$A[\\ell^n](k)\\cong(\\Z/\\ell^n\\Z)^{2g}$, and the transition map $[\\ell]:A[\\ell^{n+1}](k)\\to A[\\ell^n](k)$ is\nsurjective, since $A(k)$ is divisible by [lem-sc-isogeny-surjective]\n(an $\\ell$-th root of a point of $A[\\ell^n](k)$ lies in $A[\\ell^{n+1}](k)$). Choosing compatible bases through these surjections\nidentifies the inverse system defining $T_\\ell A$\n([def-wf-abelian-tate-module]) with the system\n$(\\Z/\\ell^n\\Z)^{2g}$ under reduction, whose limit is $\\Z_\\ell^{2g}$;\ntensoring with $\\Q_\\ell$ gives $V_\\ell A\\cong\\Q_\\ell^{2g}$.",
   "uses": [
    "lem-sc-ntorsion-etale",
    "lem-sc-isogeny-surjective",
    "def-wf-abelian-tate-module"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
